; CoreXY steps calibration — split macros (Console stays usable).
;
; Prep:
;   - Home X/Y
;   - Park X0 Y400 (room to move), or use reverse macros to back up
;
; Workflow:
;   1) Run "1 Move NE"
;   2) Measure the pencil line (ideal ~141.4 mm)
;   3) In Console:  set global.calMeasure = 141.2
;   4) Run "2 Apply Y"
;   5) Run "3 Move SE"
;   6) Measure, then:  set global.calMeasure = 141.2
;   7) Run "4 Apply X"
;
; Helpers:
;   1b Move NE reverse / 3b Move SE reverse — undo the last diagonal
;   Park X0 Y0 / Park X0 Y400 — absolute park positions

echo "=== Calibrate X/Y steps ==="
echo "Prep: Home, then Park X0 Y400"
echo "1) 1 Move NE"
echo "2) Measure (~141.4 mm)"
echo "3) Console: set global.calMeasure = <mm>"
echo "4) 2 Apply Y"
echo "5) 3 Move SE"
echo "6) Console: set global.calMeasure = <mm>"
echo "7) 4 Apply X"
echo "Helpers: 1b/3b reverse moves, Park X0 Y0 / X0 Y400"
echo "Then set Balena STEPSX/STEPSY from the final echo."
M291 P"See Console for steps. Park X0 Y400 first. Use 1-4 in order; enter mm in Console between move and apply. 1b/3b reverse if needed." R"How to calibrate" S1
